==Strategy==
While Hanayama's stats are absolutely terrifying, packing extremely high health and damage, his main flaw is his very long attack animation, taking over four seconds to complete. You can clear these five stages by pinning Hanayama to the base with meatshields and using LD attackers like [[Courier Cat]] and [[Polevaulter Cat]]. If your units aren't strong enough, you can use the Cat Cannon to reset Hanayama's attack animation and give yourself a few more seconds to beat up the base.

If you can't use this strategy, these stages are still very simple. By simply spamming meatshields, Hanayama won't be able to push at all, meaning you can chip him down slowly with backliners like [[Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Bahamut Cat]].

